  "body": "PATCH `4.21.0` → `4.21.1` (`.env.example` is a production file).\n\nThe README described the search stack as it was several releases ago. Everything shipped in 4.18.3–4.21.0 is now documented — written as **recipes**, not a settings dump.\n\n## New README sections\n\n**Giving the model full page text, not just snippets** — the highest-value capability and previously a single sentence. Now shows which switch each provider needs, how `WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS` relates to the snippet cap, which providers return text by default, and an explicit cost warning.\n\n**Restricting searches to specific sites** — the actual tool-definition shape, which six providers filter server-side, what happens on the ones that can't, and how to tell the difference from the analytics detail view.\n\n**Safe search, locale and freshness** — one topic instead of scattered per-provider trivia, including that **Firecrawl returns US results unless told otherwise**, and pointers to `TAVILY_CHUNKS_PER_SOURCE` and `FIRECRAWL_CATEGORIES=github,research` as the two options most likely to matter for coding work.\n\n**How failures are reported** — the error-code table, plus the fact that rate-limit cooldowns now follow the provider's own reset header rather than a fixed guess.\n\n**Version & Updates** — the banner now carries release notes inline.\n\n## `.env.example` drift, closed and guarded\n\nThe README points at `.env.example` for the full option list, and it had fallen behind: **none of the 13 options added in 4.20.0 were listed**, nor `WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS`.\n\nAll are now documented, and a contract test asserts every catalog option appears there — so the documented list can't silently diverge from what the admin UI offers again.\n\n## Also corrected\n\n- Parallel's row still said *\"Search API beta\"* after the v1 migration\n- The feature table still claimed *\"50+ advanced options\"* (66)\n- The analytics privacy note now says `WEBSEARCH_LOG_CAPTURE_CONTENT=false` covers **the query text itself**, not just the payloads\n\n## Verification\n\nA check over `WEBSEARCH_CATALOG` and the websearch `Settings` aliases confirms complete `.env.example` coverage — zero missing. Full suite passes except the 14 failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
