    },
    "message": "docs(websearch): document the new capabilities and close the .env.example drift\n\nThe README described the search stack as it was several releases ago. It now\ncovers what actually shipped, written as recipes rather than a settings dump:\n\n- Getting full page text to the model: which switch each provider needs, how\n  WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS relates to the snippet cap, and the cost.\n- Restricting searches to specific sites, with the tool-definition shape and\n  which providers filter server-side vs drop the filters.\n- Safe search, locale and freshness as one topic, including the fact that\n  Firecrawl returns US results unless told otherwise.\n- How failures reach the client: the error-code table, and that rate-limit\n  cooldowns follow the provider's own reset rather than a fixed guess.\n- The update banner now carrying release notes inline.\n\n.env.example had fallen behind the catalog: none of the 13 options added in\n4.20.0 were listed, and WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS was absent, while the\nREADME points at that file for the full list. All are now documented, and a\ncontract test asserts every catalog option appears there so the list cannot\nsilently fall behind the admin UI again.\n\nAlso corrected: the Parallel row still said \"Search API beta\" after the v1\nmigration, and the feature table still claimed 50+ options (66).\n\nVerification: a check over WEBSEARCH_CATALOG and the websearch Settings aliases\nconfirms complete .env.example coverage. Full suite passes except 14 failures\nthat also fail on unmodified main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
